#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
patch_L398_2_distance_figures_20261001.py -- GALLERY repo. The second of
two patches for L-398: the Solar System room's distances take JPL's own
accuracy.

Built on gallery c48f9a92e6d6094a8d25ae9413a94c17503ee50c at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/tonyquintanilla.github.io, and on the
three rows orrery patch patch_L398_1_accuracy_rows_and_skills_20261001.py
adds to constants_new.py (orrery 7a47269c09acd4d2f875f6c8d49070659c4c2ee9
at https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/palomas_orrery, plus that patch).

RUN IT AFTER THE ORRERY PATCH IS PUSHED. The gallery's maintenance run
fetches the orrery's export from GitHub. Until the orrery push, that
export has no accuracy rows, and the Pointer join check fails naming
them.

HOW TO RUN IT
    Save this file in the GALLERY repo's root folder (the one with
    interactive.html and daily_run.py). Open it in VS Code and click Run.
    No cache rebuild is needed: the page reads the accuracy links from
    data/objects_config.json directly.

WHAT A VISITOR SEES AFTER IT (?exhibit=solar-system)
    A body's distance prints to the place the larger of two errors earns:
    how far the page's arithmetic may have drifted from JPL Horizons, and
    how well JPL knows where the body is at all. With the cache of
    2026-10-01, at its own minute:
        Pluto     35.6103 AU from the Sun (5,327,220,000 km)    was 10 figures
        Neptune   29.8781 AU from the Sun (4,469,690,000 km)
        Uranus    19.4413 AU from the Sun (2,908,370,000 km)
        Saturn    9.434651 AU from the Sun (1,411,403,600 km)
        Jupiter   5.306952 AU from the Sun (793,908,700 km)
    The inner planets print whole kilometres or fewer, as before.
    Apophis keeps its distance and adds one line, your words of
    2026-10-01: "JPL's own uncertainty for this position is not yet
    included."

WHAT CHANGES
    data/objects_config.json
        Nine bodies -- Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn,
        Uranus, Neptune and the Pluto-Charon barycentre -- each gain a
        "position_accuracy" link to its group's row in the orrery's
        constants_new.py, with the values the mirror writes from it.
    interactive.html
        The room's driver passes each body's link to the text box; the
        text box adds Apophis's line; the distance functions leave the
        page for their own file.
    gallery/solar_system_figures.js        (new) the distance figures.
    documentation/smoke_solar_system_figures.js  (new) a gating check:
        six cases worked by hand, every body matched to its group's row,
        each body's distance from the served cache named with what set
        its figures, Uranus, Neptune and Pluto required at JPL's
        ten-thousands place. It breaks the real file three ways first,
        so a pass has shown it can fail.
    gallery_maintenance_run.py
        Runs the new check, and compares the new file with the live site
        after a push.

SUCCESS looks like: one "ok" line per edit and per file, then "patch
applied". FAILURE looks like: one ERROR: or ANCHOR FAIL: line, and
NOTHING is written. Undo is Discard Changes in GitHub Desktop.

Written October 1, 2026 with Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.5.
"""

import hashlib
import json
import os
import sys

